 "REPRESENTATION_CLASSES_SEARCHED": [
  "per-tensor symmetric uniform (the naive baseline every codec must beat)",
  "per-group affine with scale+zero, at group sizes 16 / 32 / 64 / 128 (spends metadata to track local range -- materially different from uniform, and the difference is decisive)",
  "grouped affine PLUS a low-rank SVD correction of its own residual (spends bytes on STRUCTURE rather than resolution)",
  "heterogeneous per-organ allocation (embedding / attention / mlp given different budgets -- an allocation lever, not a resolution lever)"
 ],
 "FINDINGS": {
  "grouping_is_the_single_largest_lever": "per-tensor uniform at 4 bits is CATASTROPHIC (perplexity 6.3 MILLION times fp32, top-1 0.000) while per-group affine at the same 4 bits costs only 1.19x perplexity at top-1 0.748. Same bit budget, ~5 million-fold difference in damage. Outlier range is what kills this body, and metadata that tracks local range is what buys it back.",
  "organ_sensitivity_is_NOT_proportional_to_mass": "crushing the MLP organ (44.3% of mass, the DOMINANT one) to 2 bits costs 2218x perplexity. Crushing the embedding organ (26.1%) to 2 bits costs 2.33x. Same budget, ~1000x difference. A naive 'attack the dominant organ' heuristic points at exactly the wrong organ here.",
  "but_the_tolerant_organ_still_imposes_a_FLOOR": "this corrects the sweep-1 reading. Embeddings at 2 bits cap achievable quality at ~1.95-2.27x perplexity and top-1 ~0.55-0.60 NO MATTER how many bits go elsewhere -- emb2 with attention AND mlp at 8 bits still lands at 1.95x / 0.593. 'Tolerant' means relatively, not cheaply. Reading sweep 1 alone would have overclaimed.",
  "low_rank_residual_did_not_pay": "adding a rank-16 SVD correction on top of grouped affine cost real metadata and did not rescue low-bit configurations (lowrank-r16-2-all: 2.837 EBPW, perplexity 1.26 MILLION x). Preserved as a FAILED hypothesis: at this scale the residual is not low-rank enough for 16 components to matter.",
  "finer_groups_help_but_cost_their_own_metadata": "g16 at 4 bits reaches top-1 0.820 but its complete EBPW is 6.0 because two fp16 scalars per 16 weights is 2 bits/weight of metadata alone -- 33% of the budget. Coarser g128 at 4 bits lands at 4.25 EBPW / top-1 0.714. The metadata share is a first-order term in the complete accounting, not a footnote."
 },
 "LADDER_VERDICT_HONEST_NEGATIVE": {
  "ladder": "<2.5 entry -> <=2.0 -> <=1.5 GRAVITY QUALIFIED -> <=1.0 PREFERRED, with capability surviving",
  "best_at_top1_>=_0.90": "grouped affine 6 bits, complete EBPW 6.500, top-1 0.9393, perplexity 1.005x",
  "best_at_top1_>=_0.70": "grouped affine 4 bits at g128, complete EBPW 4.250, top-1 0.714, perplexity 1.42x",
  "lowest_EBPW_reached_at_ANY_usable_capability": 4.25,
  "verdict": "THE LADDER IS NOT MET. Not one configuration reached even the <2.5 ENTRY rung with capability intact; everything at or below 2.5 EBPW collapsed by 5-8 orders of magnitude in perplexity with top-1 agreement at or near 0.000. Against the body's SHIPPED bf16 (16 bits) the honest win is 16 -> 6.5 EBPW (2.5x) at near-full capability, or 16 -> 4.25 (3.8x) at visibly degraded capability. Neither is a Gravity-qualified result.",
  "no_hidden_dense_fallback": "every configuration was evaluated with the dequantised weights ACTUALLY loaded into the model; there is no path where an fp32 parent supplies the answer. The restore check confirms the harness swaps real weights."
 },
 "WHY_THIS_IS_A_REAL_RESULT_AND_NOT_A_FAILURE": "the ladder targets were earned on large MoE bodies whose expert organs carry enormous redundancy -- 128 experts of which 8 fire, 94.95% of the mass in one organ. A 0.596B DENSE body has no such redundancy to spend: every weight is load-bearing, which is exactly why it is 0.6B. Learning where the ladder does NOT apply is what stops the next campaign spending GPU weeks on the wrong patient class.",
